 "note": [
  "Amharic (am) is new to the library and not yet in language_seed.py (added from the admin). Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (United Bible Societies; NT revised 2003) — the text Amharic churches of every tradition quote. Its New Testament was fetched whole from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh, USFM; ebible id `amh`). The mirror carries the NT only, so every Old Testament quotation is necessarily self_rendered in the 1962 register.",
  "Licence: the mirror records the 1962/2003 text as © UBS, attribution required, non-commercial, no derivatives. Verbatim quotation in this free library is neither commercial nor a derivative, but the credit line is owed wherever these verses render — see the PR; a founder decision before Amharic goes live.",
  "A `mined` row means an exact byte substring of the 1962 NT of at least 20 characters, measured against the finished text — not a translator's claim; its source_file names the edition, not a corpus file (no Amharic corpus exists yet). Shorter or adapted quotations are self_rendered.",
  "Divine Healing (job #3655): 32 chapters translated by fan-out and reconciled as one book. Every `mined` row was re-measured after the run (an exact 1962 NT substring of ≥20 characters inside that block, from a single-verse entry of the cited chapter ±1 verse); translator claims that failed the measure were demoted to self_rendered.",
  "Source-text caveat for reviewers: the ebible `amh` NT mirror bridges 254 verse ranges into one entry that carries only one verse's text (e.g. 1CO 6:18-20 holds only 6:18; MAT 8:16-18 only 8:18). Verses inside those ranges — here 1 Corinthians 6:19, Matthew 8:17, Hebrews 2:14, Romans 4:20, Titus 2:14 and others — could not be quoted verbatim and are self_rendered in the 1962 register; a reviewer with a printed 1962 Bible should substitute them. Its numbering also puts the second half of 1 John 3:8 under 3:9 and Matthew 11:5's close under 11:6; those quotations are verbatim and are recorded under the reference Murray cites.",
  "Editorial calls to check: Exodus 15:26, the book's refrain, is rendered «ፈዋሽህ እግዚአብሔር እኔ ነኝ» at every site (no Amharic OT available). John 11:40 is quoted verbatim from the 1962 NT, whose Amharic addresses Martha (feminine), while Murray applies it to a male believer. In chapter 11, Romans 4:19 is NOT quoted from the 1962 text, which reads that Abraham did consider his body — the reverse of the KJV sense the chapter argues from; the allusions are rendered as prose."
 ],
